WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.050
<v Andrew & Marcus>All right.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.210
<v Andrew & Marcus>Lab culture.

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.840
<v Andrew & Marcus>Death and destruction.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.390
<v Andrew & Marcus>I can just film you all the time.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.396
<v Andrew & Marcus>Don't film me, though.

00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:12.753
<v Andrew & Marcus>It's a tool to be used like
it says in the scriptures

00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:16.633
<v Andrew & Marcus>we're supposed to be things
that act and not to be

00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:20.293
<v Andrew & Marcus>acted upon If we start using
AI too much then AI starts

00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:23.937
<v Andrew & Marcus>using us and that should
be the other way around

00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:27.507
<v Andrew & Marcus>it taught me how to make the
threads pretty well that's

00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:30.207
<v Andrew & Marcus>pretty good it's funny how
bad AI's spatial reasoning

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:34.133
<v Andrew & Marcus>is it really has no concept
of like 3D space at all

00:00:34.213 --> 00:00:36.167
<v Andrew & Marcus>— it makes sense because
it's just an algorithm

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:38.307
<v Andrew & Marcus>AI is not our equal.

00:00:38.387 --> 00:00:38.907
<v Andrew & Marcus>No.

00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:41.463
<v Andrew & Marcus>It is our tool.

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:44.263
<v Andrew & Marcus>is it telling me what to
do or am I telling it what

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.313
<v Andrew & Marcus>to do you know is it acting
upon me or am I acting

00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:46.787
<v Andrew & Marcus>upon it because
